    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6095" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caesĭo</span></b> , ōnis,
			f.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A cutting</i>, <i>lopping</i>, of
			trees. castanea fere usque in alteram caesionem perennat, <i><span class="en">Col. 4, 33,
				1</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A wounding</i>, <i>killing</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Tert. Apol. 39</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
